{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019E3nszAstGvDKYL5UmDB2d","type":"tool_result","content":"=== lib.rs final state (must show asm load, write(5), != 0, 4x no_mangle) ===\n63:                \"mov {val:e}, dword ptr [{ptr}]\",\n97:#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n100:        printf(FMT_D_NL.as_ptr(), load_c_int(intNumber));\n114:#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n131:#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n134:    data.write(5);\n145:#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n147:    if useGood != 0 {\n=== 4 exported symbols present in both ===\n../c_src/build/libdriver.so: bad driver good printIntPtrLine \ntarget/release/libdriver.so: bad driver good printIntPtrLine \ntarget/debug/libdriver.so: bad driver good printIntPtrLine","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0b2d906-1f61-45f4-bd51-9b01777e437e","uuid":"91562143-d12e-4864-b61a-aac3b3e86cef","timestamp":"2026-08-28T12:24:53.431Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== lib.rs final state (must show asm load, write(5), != 0, 4x no_mangle) ===\n63:                \"mov {val:e}, dword ptr [{ptr}]\",\n97:#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n100:        printf(FMT_D_NL.as_ptr(), load_c_int(intNumber));\n114:#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n131:#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n134:    data.write(5);\n145:#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n147:    if useGood != 0 {\n=== 4 exported symbols present in both ===\n../c_src/build/libdriver.so: bad driver good printIntPtrLine \ntarget/release/libdriver.so: bad driver good printIntPtrLine \ntarget/debug/libdriver.so: bad driver good printIntPtrLine","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ki3roy3cpezb3dqp2642utpgb7yn2rxl2pyhfusds2aujjaxuqka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — **all phases pass**, and I found and fixed one real bug.\n\n## The library\n\n`c_src/src/driver.c` is a 4-function CWE-457 demo: `printIntPtrLine` prints `*p` via `printf(\"%d\\n\",...)`, `good()` prints `5`, `bad()` dereferences an **uninitialised** `int *`, and `driver(useGood)` dispatches between them.\n\n## Bug found and fixed\n\n**The debug Rust build died with `SIGABRT` where the C reads the pointer.** `printIntPtrLine` used a plain Rust deref `*intNumber`; with `debug-assertions` on, rustc emits null/alignment UB-checks that `panic!`, and a panic inside an `extern \"C\"` fn aborts the process:\n\n| input | C | Rust debug (before) |\n|---|---|---|\n| misaligned pointer into a valid buffer | prints value, exit 0 | **SIGABRT** |\n| `NULL` / unmapped address | **SIGSEGV** | **SIGABRT** |\n\nFour tests caught it. **The `--release` build passed** — testing only one profile would have missed this completely. Fixed by issuing the load as inline asm (`load_c_int`), invisible to UB-checks and identical in every profile; `read_volatile`/`read_unaligned` carry the same preconditions and would not have helped.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n**The CWE-457 rows can't be byte-compared, so I built a different gate.** `bad()` reads indeterminate memory — and the C isn't even self-consistent with itself: reaching `bad()` directly vs. via `driver(0)` prints *different* garbage. Asserting byte-equality there would be meaningless. Instead the tests assert the defect is **preserved**: the outcome is a fault or a garbage integer, never `5`, and — the key gate — **more than one distinct outcome must be observed across both call paths**. Any \"fix\" to a deterministic substitute (`data = null` → always SIGSEGV, `data = &0` → always prints `0`) collapses that to one outcome and is rejected. All three such \"fixes\" are caught as mutants.\n\n**`cargo test` does not rebuild the cdylib**, so the suite can silently pass against a stale `.so` — this actually happened and briefly made the bug look fixed. I added a staleness guard that fails loudly.\n\n## Results\n\n- **`nm -D` parity:** 0 missing symbols (debug + release), 0 undefined non-libc\n- **Phase B:** all 34 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass, randomized with fixed seed — driven through the low-level `printIntPtrLine` directly, not just the `driver()` wrapper\n- **Phase C:** all 11 `ERRORS.md` rows pass, compared on `(stdout, exit code, signal)` in child processes\n- **Features:** none declared; default and `--no-default-features` both pass\n- **Flakiness:** 12 consecutive runs, 0 failures\n- **Mutation self-check: 14/14 caught, 0 survivors** — including forced-`debug-assertions` proof that the asm fix is what provides profile-independence\n\nOne caveat on scope: the fallback path in `load_c_int` for non-x86-64/aarch64 targets relies on `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false` rather than asm, so it's the one part not machine-verified here.\n\nArtifacts in `translation/`: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `tests/differential.rs`, `examples/runner.rs`, `mutation_check.sh`, `verify_all.sh`. `c_src/` untouched apart from the `build/` directory."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":658,"cache_read_input_tokens":115699,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":658,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0b2d906-1f61-45f4-bd51-9b01777e437e","uuid":"1e8324bf-3419-41a7-aee8-440484f49d2f","timestamp":"2026-08-28T12:25:09.471Z"}
