luding forced-`debug-assertions` proof that the asm fix is what provides profile-independence\n\nOne caveat on scope: the fallback path in `load_c_int` for non-x86-64/aarch64 targets relies on `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false` rather than asm, so it's the one part not machine-verified here.\n\nArtifacts in `translation/`: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `tests/differential.rs`, `examples/runner.rs`, `mutation_check.sh`, `verify_all.sh`. `c_src/` untouched apart from the `build/` directory.","ttft_ms":3258,"ttft_stream_ms":3071,"time_to_request_ms":48,"type":"result","duration_ms":1103464,"uuid":"2e03954b-76df-4c4f-b77b-b2209a10e4f6","queued_turn_count":0}
